    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d795">

                <pb facs="0826" n="776" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg776"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. Riddle.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 177.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I append a copy of telegrams relative to
                    the passport of Adam Aivazian and his right to claim such protection as the
                    United States can give to citizens who were former subjects of Turkey and who
                    have returned to Ottoman jurisdiction.</p>
                <p>As Mr. Terrell appears to have pledged himself to take into consideration
                    Aivazian’s acts in Turkey in determining whether he is entitled to protection,
                    it is proper that the legation should be afforded full opportunity to ascertain
                    the nature of the acts imputed to this man.</p>
                <p>I inclose a copy of Mr. Aivazian’s application for a passport.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d795-f1"/></p>
                <p>Referring you to instruction No. 162 of the 29th ultimo, more specifically
                    setting forth the ground upon which your legation should be afforded all proper
                    facilities for arriving at the facts in Aivazian’s case, I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
